<title>BELGIUM: Belgium cuts liquidity at money tender.</title>
<headline>Belgium cuts liquidity at money tender.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian National Bank cut liquidity at its fixed-rate tender for seven-day advances.</p>
<p>Details -</p>
<p>    Value date 22/01	  expiry on 29/01</p>
<p>    Amount allotted	   14.450 bln bfr    (15.500 bln *)</p>
<p>    Interest rate	     3.00 pct	    (3.00 pct **)</p>
<p>    Total amount of bids    14.450 bln bfr</p>
<p>Percentage of bids accepted  100</p>
<p>* amount draining from the money market on 22/01</p>
<p>** interest rate at previous tender</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
